1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,212
Do you need receipts for taxes?

2
00:00:02,512 --> 00:00:04,230
Short answer: you need proof.

3
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:05,497
And a receipt is usually

4
00:00:05,497 --> 00:00:06,898
the best proof you’ve got.

5
00:00:07,348 --> 00:00:08,575
The IRS wants records

6
00:00:08,575 --> 00:00:10,275
that back up your return.

7
00:00:10,275 --> 00:00:11,740
For a business expense,

8
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,869
that’s five things.

9
00:00:13,169 --> 00:00:14,475
Who you paid. How much.

10
00:00:14,475 --> 00:00:15,960
Proof you paid. The date.

11
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:16,969
And what it was for.

12
00:00:17,419 --> 00:00:18,945
Here’s what most people miss.

13
00:00:18,945 --> 00:00:20,239
A receipt usually shows

14
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:21,159
the first four.

15
00:00:21,459 --> 00:00:22,730
The fifth, what it was for?

16
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:23,875
Only you know that.

17
00:00:24,325 --> 00:00:25,530
So snap the receipt,

18
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:27,255
and add one line about why.

19
00:00:27,255 --> 00:00:28,600
That’s a complete record.

20
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,055
Find us at receipt-nest.com,

21
00:00:31,055 --> 00:00:32,799
on the App Store and Google Play.
